%I A399271 #11 Aug 25 2026 17:52:23
%S A399271 1,1,0,648,1795107264
%N A399271 a(n) is the number of n X n matrices whose entries are a permutation of 1, ..., n^2, such that the determinant of the matrix is equal to the product of its terms on the main diagonal.
%C A399271 An estimate for the next terms, based on 10^10 randomly permuted matrices each, is a(5) approximately equal to 2*10^19 and a(6) approximately equal to 4*10^33.
%e A399271 a(2) = 0, because none of the matrices with positive determinant [2, 3; 1, 4], [2, 4; 1, 3], [3, 1, 2, 4] and their determinant-preserving isomorphisms satisfies the criterion; 2*4-3*1 = 5 != 2*4, 2*3-4*1 = 2 != 2*3, 3*4-1*2 = 10 != 3*4.
%e A399271 One of the a(3)=648 3X3 matrices is
%e A399271   [3, 5, 1;
%e A399271    2, 8, 6;
%e A399271    7, 4, 9] with determinant 216 = 3*8*9.
%e A399271 .
%e A399271 A matrix matching the condition for n=4 is
%e A399271   [9,  7, 8, 14;
%e A399271   13, 12, 3,  5;
%e A399271   16, 15, 4, 11;
%e A399271   10,  2, 1,  6] with determinant 2592 = 9*12*4*6.
%o A399271 (PARI) \\ Not suitable for n>3.
%o A399271 a399271(n) = if(n<2, 1, my(A=matrix(n,n), k=0); forperm(n^2, p, my(m=0); for(i=1,n, for(j=1, n, A[i,j]=p[m++])); if(prod(m=1, n, A[m,m])==matdet(A), k++)); k);
%Y A399271 Cf. A085000 (see there for related CROSSREFS), A180087.
%K A399271 nonn,hard,more,bref,new
%O A399271 0,4
%A A399271 _Hugo Pfoertner_, Aug 25 2026
